-- int-tests-fixtures.l4: the named people, licences, systems, councils and index readings used by the int-tests- modules.
-- No assertion is made here.  Every date and figure is chosen by the test author to put a scenario on one side of an edge; none is a
-- fact of the Law, which appears only in the assertions, each with the provision that gives it (see expectations.md in the work
-- directory, written before any of these modules ran).

§ `Fixtures: people`

`fixture: Dana, an individual` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference for the person` IS "il-dana"
    `kind of person` IS `an individual`

`fixture: Noa, an individual` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference for the person` IS "il-noa"
    `kind of person` IS `an individual`

`fixture: Hans, an individual and a foreign expert` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference for the person` IS "de-hans"
    `kind of person` IS `an individual`

`fixture: Ofek Ltd, a corporation` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference for the person` IS "il-ofek-ltd"
    `kind of person` IS `a corporation`

`fixture: Kar-Kor Ltd, a corporation` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference for the person` IS "il-karkor-ltd"
    `kind of person` IS `a corporation`

`fixture: a clean record` MEANS `Record of offences` WITH
    `convicted of a criminal offence` IS FALSE
    `convicted of a disciplinary offence` IS FALSE
    `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet` IS FALSE
    `a disciplinary complaint is pending with no final judgment` IS FALSE

§ `Fixtures: licences`

GIVEN holder IS A Person
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
      granted IS A DATE
GIVETH A Licence
`fixture: an ordinary licence held by` holder `of kind` kind `granted on` granted MEANS
    Licence WITH
        `the holder` IS holder
        `the kind of licence` IS kind
        `a temporary licence under section 9` IS FALSE
        `granted on` IS granted
        `renewed on` IS EMPTY
        `validity ends on, as recorded` IS NOTHING
        `revoked on` IS NOTHING
        `suspended from` IS NOTHING
        `suspended until` IS NOTHING

GIVEN holder IS A Person
      granted IS A DATE
      lastDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A Licence
`fixture: a temporary licence held by` holder `granted on` granted `and recorded to end on` lastDay MEANS
    Licence WITH
        `the holder` IS holder
        `the kind of licence` IS `grade 3 licence`
        `a temporary licence under section 9` IS TRUE
        `granted on` IS granted
        `renewed on` IS EMPTY
        `validity ends on, as recorded` IS JUST lastDay
        `revoked on` IS NOTHING
        `suspended from` IS NOTHING
        `suspended until` IS NOTHING

GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      revoked IS A DATE
GIVETH A Licence
`fixture: the licence` licence `after the register records it revoked on` revoked MEANS
    Licence WITH
        `the holder` IS licence's `the holder`
        `the kind of licence` IS licence's `the kind of licence`
        `a temporary licence under section 9` IS licence's `a temporary licence under section 9`
        `granted on` IS licence's `granted on`
        `renewed on` IS licence's `renewed on`
        `validity ends on, as recorded` IS licence's `validity ends on, as recorded`
        `revoked on` IS JUST revoked
        `suspended from` IS licence's `suspended from`
        `suspended until` IS licence's `suspended until`

GIVEN licence IS A Licence
      firstDay IS A DATE
      lastDay IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A Licence
`fixture: the licence` licence `after the register records it suspended from` firstDay `until` lastDay MEANS
    Licence WITH
        `the holder` IS licence's `the holder`
        `the kind of licence` IS licence's `the kind of licence`
        `a temporary licence under section 9` IS licence's `a temporary licence under section 9`
        `granted on` IS licence's `granted on`
        `renewed on` IS licence's `renewed on`
        `validity ends on, as recorded` IS licence's `validity ends on, as recorded`
        `revoked on` IS licence's `revoked on`
        `suspended from` IS JUST firstDay
        `suspended until` IS lastDay

§ `Fixtures: systems and acts`

GIVEN kilowatts IS A NUMBER
      designation IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`fixture: a system of` kilowatts `kilowatts using refrigerant` designation MEANS
    `Cooling system` WITH
        `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS kilowatts
        `refrigerants` IS LIST (Refrigerant WITH
                                    `designation` IS designation
                                    `use of the refrigerant is permitted by law` IS TRUE)

`fixture: facts with neither limit satisfied` MEANS `Facts about an act for the limits of First Schedule items` WITH
    `the parts connected are integral control and monitoring accessories only` IS FALSE
    `the electrical work is done in the integral electrical system only` IS FALSE

`fixture: facts with the electrical limit satisfied` MEANS `Facts about an act for the limits of First Schedule items` WITH
    `the parts connected are integral control and monitoring accessories only` IS FALSE
    `the electrical work is done in the integral electrical system only` IS TRUE

GIVEN person IS A Person
      licences IS A LIST OF Licence
      day IS A DATE
      system IS A `Cooling system`
      activity IS A `First Schedule activity`
GIVETH A `Situation of one piece of work`
`fixture: the work of` person `holding` licences `on` day `on the system` system `amounting to` activity MEANS
    `Situation of one piece of work` WITH
        `the person who does the work` IS person
        `licences of the person` IS licences
        `the day of the work` IS day
        `the cooling system worked on` IS system
        `the activity the act amounts to` IS JUST activity
        `the limits of the item` IS `fixture: facts with neither limit satisfied`
        `a restriction covering this work` IS NOTHING
        `the system is of a class exempted by an order under section 3(b)` IS FALSE
        `the person breached a licence condition other than the training duty` IS FALSE
        `a provision under the Law was breached by the work` IS FALSE
        `the training records` IS EMPTY

GIVEN s IS A `Situation of one piece of work`
      records IS A LIST OF `Training record under one licence`
GIVETH A `Situation of one piece of work`
`fixture: training records added to the situation` s `being` records MEANS
    `Situation of one piece of work` WITH
        `the person who does the work` IS s's `the person who does the work`
        `licences of the person` IS s's `licences of the person`
        `the day of the work` IS s's `the day of the work`
        `the cooling system worked on` IS s's `the cooling system worked on`
        `the activity the act amounts to` IS s's `the activity the act amounts to`
        `the limits of the item` IS s's `the limits of the item`
        `a restriction covering this work` IS s's `a restriction covering this work`
        `the system is of a class exempted by an order under section 3(b)` IS s's `the system is of a class exempted by an order under section 3(b)`
        `the person breached a licence condition other than the training duty` IS s's `the person breached a licence condition other than the training duty`
        `a provision under the Law was breached by the work` IS s's `a provision under the Law was breached by the work`
        `the training records` IS records

GIVEN s IS A `Situation of one piece of work`
      limits IS A `Facts about an act for the limits of First Schedule items`
GIVETH A `Situation of one piece of work`
`fixture: limits of the item set in the situation` s `to` limits MEANS
    `Situation of one piece of work` WITH
        `the person who does the work` IS s's `the person who does the work`
        `licences of the person` IS s's `licences of the person`
        `the day of the work` IS s's `the day of the work`
        `the cooling system worked on` IS s's `the cooling system worked on`
        `the activity the act amounts to` IS s's `the activity the act amounts to`
        `the limits of the item` IS limits
        `a restriction covering this work` IS s's `a restriction covering this work`
        `the system is of a class exempted by an order under section 3(b)` IS s's `the system is of a class exempted by an order under section 3(b)`
        `the person breached a licence condition other than the training duty` IS s's `the person breached a licence condition other than the training duty`
        `a provision under the Law was breached by the work` IS s's `a provision under the Law was breached by the work`
        `the training records` IS s's `the training records`

GIVEN s IS A `Situation of one piece of work`
GIVETH A `Situation of one piece of work`
`fixture: the system exempted by an order in the situation` s MEANS
    `Situation of one piece of work` WITH
        `the person who does the work` IS s's `the person who does the work`
        `licences of the person` IS s's `licences of the person`
        `the day of the work` IS s's `the day of the work`
        `the cooling system worked on` IS s's `the cooling system worked on`
        `the activity the act amounts to` IS s's `the activity the act amounts to`
        `the limits of the item` IS s's `the limits of the item`
        `a restriction covering this work` IS s's `a restriction covering this work`
        `the system is of a class exempted by an order under section 3(b)` IS TRUE
        `the person breached a licence condition other than the training duty` IS s's `the person breached a licence condition other than the training duty`
        `a provision under the Law was breached by the work` IS s's `a provision under the Law was breached by the work`
        `the training records` IS s's `the training records`

GIVEN operator IS A Person
      engaged IS A LIST OF Licence
      day IS A DATE
      system IS A `Cooling system`
      activity IS A `First Schedule activity`
GIVETH A `Situation of one engagement`
`fixture: the engagement by` operator `of a person holding` engaged `on` day `for work on the system` system `amounting to` activity MEANS
    `Situation of one engagement` WITH
        `the operator` IS operator
        `facts about the operator` IS `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems` WITH
            `engages another person on a regular basis to perform work on cooling systems` IS TRUE
            `owns or manages a business that offers the performance of work on cooling systems to the public` IS FALSE
        `licences of the engaged person` IS engaged
        `the day of the engagement` IS day
        `the cooling system worked on` IS system
        `the activity the act amounts to` IS JUST activity
        `the limits of the item` IS `fixture: facts with neither limit satisfied`

§ `Fixtures: the Council`

m1 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m1", TRUE
m2 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m2", FALSE
m3 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m3", FALSE
m4 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m4", FALSE
m5 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m5", FALSE
m6 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m6", FALSE
m7 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m7", FALSE
m8 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m8", FALSE
m9 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m9", FALSE
m10 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m10", FALSE
m11 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m11", FALSE

`fixture: the eleven members serving` MEANS LIST m1, m2, m3, m4, m5, m6, m7, m8, m9, m10, m11

-- Fields: serving members | every member duly summoned | present | voted for | voted against.
`fixture: a meeting with six present including the chair, three for and two against` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `fixture: the eleven members serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5")
`fixture: a meeting with five present including the chair, four for and one against` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `fixture: the eleven members serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4"), (LIST "m5")

`fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter` MEANS `int — a consultation on an individual matter whose advice came from` (`the Council at a meeting` WITH `the meeting` IS `fixture: a meeting with six present including the chair, three for and two against`)
`fixture: a consultation on an individual matter at a meeting without a quorum` MEANS `int — a consultation on an individual matter whose advice came from` (`the Council at a meeting` WITH `the meeting` IS `fixture: a meeting with five present including the chair, four for and one against`)
`fixture: a valid consultation on an exemption` MEANS `int — a consultation on an exemption whose advice came from` (`the Council at a meeting` WITH `the meeting` IS `fixture: a meeting with six present including the chair, three for and two against`)
`fixture: a consultation on an exemption at a meeting without a quorum` MEANS `int — a consultation on an exemption whose advice came from` (`the Council at a meeting` WITH `the meeting` IS `fixture: a meeting with five present including the chair, four for and one against`)

GIVEN procedure IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Consultation of the Council`
`fixture: a consultation on an individual matter advised by a subcommittee, the procedure being` procedure MEANS
    `int — a consultation on an individual matter whose advice came from` (`a subcommittee that advises the Council` WITH
        `the Council delegated its powers in the function to the subcommittee` IS TRUE
        `the subcommittee proceeded as the procedure fixed by the Council requires` IS procedure)

§ `Fixtures: index readings and calendars`

-- List A, for the sanctions of Chapter 6 (section 47(b)).  Fields: year | month | published on | value.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      published IS A DATE
      value IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`fixture: the reading for year` year `and month` month `published on` published `valued` value MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH
        `year of the index` IS year
        `month of the index` IS month
        `published on` IS published
        `value of the index` IS value

`fixture: the index readings for the sanctions` MEANS
    LIST `fixture: the reading for year` 2024 `and month` 11 `published on` (YMD 2024 12 15) `valued` 100
       , `fixture: the reading for year` 2025 `and month` 11 `published on` (YMD 2025 12 15) `valued` 102
       , `fixture: the reading for year` 2026 `and month` 11 `published on` (YMD 2026 12 15) `valued` 102
       , `fixture: the reading for year` 2027 `and month` 11 `published on` (YMD 2027 12 15) `valued` 102
       , `fixture: the reading for year` 2028 `and month` 11 `published on` (YMD 2028 12 15) `valued` 102
       , `fixture: the reading for year` 2029 `and month` 11 `published on` (YMD 2029 12 15) `valued` 102

-- List F, for the fees of regulation 3(a): published in the month before the commencement (June 2025), in November 2025 and in November 2026.
`fixture: the index readings for the fees` MEANS
    LIST `fixture: the reading for year` 2025 `and month` 5 `published on` (YMD 2025 6 15) `valued` 100
       , `fixture: the reading for year` 2025 `and month` 10 `published on` (YMD 2025 11 15) `valued` 101.25
       , `fixture: the reading for year` 2026 `and month` 10 `published on` (YMD 2026 11 15) `valued` 102.515625

`fixture: no day of rest at all` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

§ `Fixtures: commencement facts`

-- The facts "as the sources give them" (no regulation under s.46), and the hypothesis used to price violations: regulations under
-- s.46 in force from 1 June 2026, so that Chapter 6 commences with the later limb, 16 January 2027.
`fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46` MEANS `int — the facts that fix the commencement, section 46 regulations being in force from` (YMD 2026 6 1)

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Facts for pricing a violation`
`fixture: the pricing of a violation that did not continue and has no earlier violation, updated on` day MEANS
    `Facts for pricing a violation` WITH
        `the violation continued from` IS NOTHING
        `the last day the violation continued` IS day
        `the previous violations of the violator` IS EMPTY
        `the day on which the amount is updated` IS day
        `the year of the first update day` IS 2026
        `the index readings` IS `fixture: the index readings for the sanctions`

§ `Fixtures: applicants, applications and grants`

GIVEN person IS A Person
GIVETH AN Applicant
`fixture: an applicant with no prior training, being` person MEANS
    Applicant WITH
        `the person` IS person
        `of full age` IS TRUE
        `an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
        `an Israeli resident` IS TRUE
        `record of offences` IS `fixture: a clean record`
        `licences held` IS EMPTY
        `certificates held` IS EMPTY
        `registered as a certified technician in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
        `registered as a certified practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
        `completed a study programme that includes the complement course` IS FALSE
        `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch` IS FALSE
        `periods of work on cooling systems` IS EMPTY
        `holds a valid electrician licence of a kind listed in the Electricity Regulations` IS FALSE
        `holds a valid working-at-height approval` IS FALSE

GIVEN person IS A Person
      periods IS A LIST OF `Period of work on cooling systems`
GIVETH AN Applicant
`fixture: an applicant with only the periods of work, being` person `and the periods` periods MEANS
    Applicant WITH
        `the person` IS person
        `of full age` IS TRUE
        `an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
        `an Israeli resident` IS TRUE
        `record of offences` IS `fixture: a clean record`
        `licences held` IS EMPTY
        `certificates held` IS EMPTY
        `registered as a certified technician in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
        `registered as a certified practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
        `completed a study programme that includes the complement course` IS FALSE
        `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch` IS FALSE
        `periods of work on cooling systems` IS periods
        `holds a valid electrician licence of a kind listed in the Electricity Regulations` IS FALSE
        `holds a valid working-at-height approval` IS FALSE

GIVEN applicant IS AN Applicant
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH AN Application
`fixture: an application by` applicant `for a` kind `on` day MEANS
    Application WITH
        `the applicant` IS applicant
        `the kind of licence sought` IS kind
        `an application to renew` IS FALSE
        `an application for a temporary licence` IS FALSE
        `the day of the application` IS day

`fixture: a programme the Registrar consented to` MEANS `Study programme under section 19(b)` OF "diploma", TRUE, TRUE
`fixture: a programme the Registrar did not consent to` MEANS `Study programme under section 19(b)` OF "diploma", TRUE, FALSE

-- A grade 1 application in the ordinary case, the Fees Regulations as made: the training was completed in the programme given.
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      programme IS A MAYBE `Study programme under section 19(b)`
      paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Facts of a grant under section 6`
`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` application `with the programme being` programme `and the amount paid being` paid MEANS
    `Facts of a grant under section 6` WITH
        `the application` IS application
        `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS FALSE
        `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS TRUE
        `the programme the applicant completed` IS programme
        `the foreign qualification relied on` IS NOTHING
        `the vintage of the Fees Regulations` IS `the Fees Regulations as made`
        `the amount paid for the licence` IS paid
        `the index readings` IS EMPTY

GIVEN application IS AN Application
      paid IS A NUMBER
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A `Facts of a grant under section 6`
`fixture: a grant with the readings on` application `with the amount paid being` paid `and the readings being` readings MEANS
    `Facts of a grant under section 6` WITH
        `the application` IS application
        `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS FALSE
        `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS TRUE
        `the programme the applicant completed` IS JUST `fixture: a programme the Registrar consented to`
        `the foreign qualification relied on` IS NOTHING
        `the vintage of the Fees Regulations` IS `the Fees Regulations as made`
        `the amount paid for the licence` IS paid
        `the index readings` IS readings

-- A grant that rests on a foreign qualification: no Israeli training was completed and no programme.
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      consultation IS A `Consultation of the Council`
GIVETH A `Facts of a grant under section 6`
`fixture: a grant on a foreign degree on` application `after the consultation` consultation MEANS
    `Facts of a grant under section 6` WITH
        `the application` IS application
        `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS FALSE
        `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS FALSE
        `the programme the applicant completed` IS NOTHING
        `the foreign qualification relied on` IS JUST (`Foreign qualification relied on` WITH
            `the foreign qualification` IS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "degree", TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
            `what the Registrar considered` IS `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
            `the consultation of the Council` IS consultation)
        `the vintage of the Fees Regulations` IS `the Fees Regulations as made`
        `the amount paid for the licence` IS 284
        `the index readings` IS EMPTY
